    imageHint: "Muravanka fortified church with round corner towers",
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Die Kirche der Geburt der Heiligen Jungfrau Maria in Murawanka ist ein faszinierendes Meisterwerk der sakralen Verteidigungsarchitektur des 16. Jahrhunderts. Erbaut zwischen 1516 und 1542, kombiniert dieses seltene architektonische Juwel harmonisch die Funktionen eines spirituellen Gotteshauses mit denen einer fast uneinnehmbaren militärischen Festung. Das auffälligste Merkmal des Backsteinbaus sind seine vier robusten, runden Ecktürme, die mit zahlreichen Schießscharten ausgestattet sind. Die extrem dicken Mauern der Kirche waren darauf ausgelegt, Artilleriebeschuss standzuhalten, was das Gebäude im Laufe der Jahrhunderte vor der Zerstörung durch schwedische und russische Truppen rettete. Im Inneren beeindruckt die Kirche mit feinen Sterngewölben, die im Kontrast zu ihrem wehrhaften Äußeren stehen. Die Murawanka-Kirche ist ein herausragendes Beispiel der belarussischen Gotik mit Elementen der Renaissance.",
      hu: "A muravankai Kisboldogasszony-templom a 16. századi szakrális és védelmi építészet egyik legkülönlegesebb és legértékesebb fennmaradt alkotása. Az 1516 és 1542 között emelt épület ritka mestermű, amely tökéletesen ötvözi a vallási funkciót egy szinte bevehetetlen katonai erődítmény jellegzetességeivel. A robusztus téglaépület legszembetűnőbb elemei a négy sarkán elhelyezkedő vaskos, kerek saroktornyok, amelyeket lőrésekkel láttak el. A templom rendkívül vastag falait úgy tervezték, hogy ellenálljanak a tüzérségi támadásoknak, aminek köszönhetően az évszázadok során sikeresen átvészelte a svéd és orosz csapatok ostromait. A zord, katonás külsővel éles ellentétben a belső tér gyönyörű, finoman kidolgozott csillagboltozatos mennyezettel rendelkezik. A muravankai erődtemplom a fehérorosz gótika és a korai reneszánsz páratlan találkozása.",
      ro: "Biserica Nașterea Maicii Domnului din Muravanka este o capodoperă fascinantă a arhitecturii sacre defensive din secolul al XVI-lea. Construită între 1516 și 1542, această bijuterie arhitecturală rară combină armonios funcția spirituală a unui lăcaș de cult cu structura unei fortărețe militare aproape inexpugnabile. Cea mai proeminentă trăsătură a edificiului din cărămidă este prezența celor patru turnuri de colț rotunde și robuste, prevăzute cu numeroase metereze. Zidurile extrem de groase au fost proiectate pentru a rezista tirurilor de artilerie, ceea ce a salvat clădirea de la distrugere în timpul războaielor cu trupele suedeze și rusești de-a lungul secolelor. În interior, biserica impresionează prin bolțile sale stelate delicate, care contrastează puternic cu exteriorul său fortificat, reprezentând un exemplu remarcabil de gotic belarus cu influențe renascentiste.",
      en: "The Church of the Nativity of the Blessed Virgin Mary in Muravanka is a fascinating masterpiece of 16th-century sacral defense architecture. Constructed between 1516 and 1542, this rare architectural jewel harmoniously blends the spiritual functions of a place of worship with the robust attributes of an almost impregnable military fortress. The most striking feature of the red brick building is its four sturdy, round corner towers, which are heavily equipped with multiple tiers of embrasures (loopholes). The exceptionally thick walls of the church were specifically designed to withstand artillery fire, a feature that saved the structure from destruction by Swedish and Russian forces over the centuries. Inside, the church contrasts its harsh exterior with delicate stellar vaults, making it an outstanding example of Belarusian Gothic architecture mixed with early Renaissance elements."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Built between 1516 and 1542 using a unique combination of Gothic and Renaissance styles.", "Features four distinct cylindrical corner defense towers equipped with loopholes.", "The walls of the church reach an impressive thickness of up to 2 meters.", "The building was heavily damaged by Swedish forces in 1656 during wartime.", "Underwent a significant architectural modification and restoration in the late 19th century.", "The interior is celebrated for its highly detailed and elegant crystal cell vaults.", "Served as both a spiritual center and a safe refuge for villagers during enemy attacks."],
      hu: [],
      ro: [],
      en: []
    }
