    name: { de: "Große Synagoge von Slonim", hu: "Szlonimi nagyzsinagóga", ro: "Sinagoga Mare din Slonim", en: "Slonim Great Synagogue"},
    image: "/poi-images/belarus-slonim-great-synagogue-landmarks-v2.webp",
    coords: [25.3192, 53.094],
    coords: [25.3192, 53.094],
    description: {
      de: "Die Große Synagoge von Slonim ist eine der ältesten erhaltenen Barocksynagogen in Belarus. Sie wurde 1642 erbaut und diente einst als Festungsbau.",
      hu: "A szlonimi nagyzsinagóga Fehéroroszország egyik legrégebbi fennmaradt zsinagógája. Az 1642-ben épült barokk épület védelmi célokat is szolgált.",
      ro: "Sinagoga Mare din Slonim este unul dintre cele mai vechi lăcașuri de cult evreiești din Belarus. A fost construită în 1642 în stil baroc.",
      en: "The Slonim Great Synagogue is one of the oldest surviving synagogue buildings in Belarus. Built in 1642, it originally featured defensive elements.",
    },
    facts: {
      de: ["Wurde im Jahr 1642 während der Herrschaft von Władysław IV. Wasa erbaut.", "Das Gebäude besitzt mächtige Mauern und ein hohes Mansarddach.", "Im Inneren sind Stuckarbeiten aus dem 17. Jahrhundert erhalten.", "Diente nach 1945 als Lagerhaus und verfiel zusehends."],
      hu: ["1642-ben épült IV. Ulászló lengyel király uralkodása alatt.", "Vastag falaival erődtemplomként is funkcionált.", "A belső térben 17. századi stukkók és freskók láthatók.", "A szovjet időszakban raktárként használták, állapota sokat romlott."],
      ro: ["Construită în 1642 în timpul domniei lui Vladislav al IV-lea.", "Edificiul are ziduri groase și acoperiș înalt de tip mansardă.", "Interiorul păstrează fresce și stucaturi din secolul al XVII-lea.", "A fost utilizată ca depozit în perioada sovietică."],
      en: ["Constructed in 1642 during the reign of Wladyslaw IV Vasa.", "The building features thick walls and a high mansard roof.", "The interior retains rare 17th-century stucco and wall paintings.", "It was used as a warehouse during the Soviet era."],
    },
    imageHint: "Slonim Great Synagogue old building",
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Die Große Synagoge in Slonim ist ein bemerkenswertes und ergreifendes historisches Denkmal, das an die einst blühende und große jüdische Gemeinde der Region erinnert. Das mächtige Gebäude wurde 1642 im reifen Barockstil errichtet und ist eine der wenigen erhaltenen Synagogen in Belarus aus dieser Zeit. Ihre dicken Backsteinmauern, schmalen Fenster und das hohe Mansardendach lassen erkennen, dass sie ursprünglich nicht nur religiösen Zwecken, sondern auch der Verteidigung der Stadt diente. Das Innere der Synagoge bewahrt trotz starkem Verfall immer noch Spuren einstiger Pracht: Die einzigartigen und detaillierten Stuckarbeiten, Reste von Fresken und der prunkvolle, von Säulen gestützte steinerne Bima (Altar) zeugen vom handwerklichen Können des 17. Jahrhunderts. Nach dem Holocaust wurde das Gebäude während der Sowjetzeit profan als Lagerhaus genutzt. Heute laufen Bemühungen, die verfallende Struktur zu stabilisieren und als wichtiges kulturelles Erbe zu erhalten.",
      hu: "A szlonimi nagyzsinagóga egy kiemelkedő és egyben megrázó történelmi műemlék, amely a régió egykor virágzó és népes zsidó közösségének állít emléket. Az impozáns épületet 1642-ben emelték érett barokk stílusban, és egyike Fehéroroszország nagyon kevés fennmaradt 17. századi zsinagógájának. A vastag téglafalak, a magasan elhelyezett, keskeny ablakok és a jellegzetes manszárdtető egyértelműen arra utalnak, hogy az épület vallási funkciója mellett a város védelmi rendszerének is fontos részét képezte. A zsinagóga belső tere a súlyos pusztulás ellenére is őrzi egykori pompájának nyomait: az egyedülállóan részletgazdag, 17. századi stukkók, a freskók maradványai és a lenyűgöző, oszlopokon nyugvó kőbima (Tóra-olvasó emelvény) mind a korabeli kézművesek zsenialitását dicsérik. A holokauszt után a szovjet érában az épületet raktárként hasznosították; napjainkban nemzetközi erőfeszítések zajlanak a megmentésére.",
      ro: "Sinagoga Mare din Slonim este un monument istoric remarcabil și emoționant, servind ca mărturie tăcută a comunității evreiești, odinioară vibrantă și numeroasă în regiune. Această structură masivă a fost construită în anul 1642, într-un stil baroc matur, și reprezintă una dintre puținele sinagogi din Belarus care au supraviețuit din acea epocă. Zidurile sale groase din cărămidă, ferestrele înguste și acoperișul înalt tip mansardă dezvăluie faptul că edificiul a fost conceput inițial nu doar ca loc de cult, ci și ca o fortăreață defensivă. În ciuda degradării severe, interiorul păstrează încă urme ale splendorii de altădată: stucaturi unice, extrem de detaliate din secolul al XVII-lea, fragmente de fresce și o bimah (bima) centrală din piatră sprijinită pe coloane elegante. După Holocaust, clădirea a fost folosită ca depozit în perioada sovietică, iar astăzi există campanii internaționale pentru restaurarea sa.",
      en: "The Great Synagogue in Slonim is a remarkable and deeply poignant historical monument, standing as a silent witness to the once-thriving and populous Jewish community of the region. Constructed in 1642 in a mature Baroque architectural style, this massive structure is one of the very few surviving 17th-century synagogues in Belarus. Its thick brick walls, high narrow windows, and prominent mansard roof clearly indicate that the building was originally designed to serve a dual purpose: as a place of worship and as a defensive fortress for the town. Despite severe decay, the interior still remarkably preserves traces of its former splendor. Visitors can see unique, highly detailed 17th-century stucco work, remnants of painted frescoes, and a magnificent central stone bimah supported by elegant columns. Following the Holocaust, the building was secularized and used as a warehouse during the Soviet era; today, there are active international efforts to save and restore this crucial heritage site."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Constructed in 1642 during the reign of King Wladyslaw IV Vasa of Poland.", "Built in the Baroque style but with heavy, thick walls designed for military defense.", "The interior features an exceptionally rare, well-preserved monumental stone bimah.", "Decorated with intricate 17th-century stucco reliefs featuring animals and floral motifs.", "The Jewish community of Slonim was almost entirely eradicated during the Holocaust.", "Survived World War II but was heavily neglected and used as a warehouse under Soviet rule.", "Sold to a private individual in 2020 who initiated an international campaign to restore it."],
      hu: [],
      ro: [],
      en: []
    }
